The RKE2 server service is healthy at the systemd level:

```text
Active: active (running)
```

and the RKE2 process, containerd, and kubelet are running. 

RKE2 also successfully established its remotedialer/proxy connection to:

```text
10.174.161.22:9345
```

and ultimately reports:

```text
Connected to proxy
Remotedialer connected to proxy
```

So the transient:

```text
websocket: close 1006
```

is not the primary problem because RKE2 reconnects immediately afterward. 

The important failure is here:

```text
Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - no CNI

ok: [master01] => (item=master01)
FAILED - RETRYING...
```

That means the role got through installation and startup, but its Kubernetes readiness condition is not being satisfied for another expected node or cluster condition. 

