node-ip: 10.174.161.22
token: <cluster-token>
cni: none
```

There normally should **not** be a `server:` pointing to another master on the very first bootstrap server.

## Your `--limit master01` matters

You launched:

```bash
ansible-playbook \
  -i inventory/dev/hosts.ini \
  playbooks/deploy-rke2.yml \
  --limit=master01
```

Yet the role still knows about and delegates operations to:

```text
master02 10.174.161.23
master03 10.174.161.24
```

The output proves that:

```text
master01 -> master02(10.174.161.23)
master01 -> master03(10.174.161.24)
```



This matters because `lablabs.rke2` is designed around the **whole cluster inventory**. `--limit master01` does not necessarily turn the cluster definition into a one-node cluster. The role can still iterate over all servers from inventory variables/groups.

So I would **not continue repeatedly running the full role with `--limit master01`** until we establish precisely what the wait task is checking.

Inspect that task:

```bash
sed -n '1,260p' \
  roles/lablabs.rke2/tasks/remaining_nodes.yml
```

And specifically:

```bash
grep -nA25 -B10 \
  'Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - no CNI' \
  roles/lablabs.rke2/tasks/remaining_nodes.yml
```

That command is especially important. It will show exactly what condition is retrying.

