## My recommended deployment sequence

For this air-gapped build, I would deploy more deterministically:

```text
1. master01
      ↓
   validate API
      ↓
   validate etcd
      ↓
   validate containerd
      ↓
   validate registry access
      ↓
2. master02
      ↓
3. master03
      ↓
   validate 3-member etcd
      ↓
4. workers
      ↓
5. Cilium
      ↓
6. verify all nodes Ready
```

Since Cilium is intentionally installed separately, don't use ordinary Kubernetes `Ready` as the only bootstrap success criterion before Cilium exists. A node can legitimately remain `NotReady` because:

```text
NetworkPluginNotReady
cni plugin not initialized
```

while RKE2, kubelet, containerd, API server and etcd are otherwise healthy.

